WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.940
If Christ has freed me from sin,

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.740
why am I still tempted?

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.620
Romans six distinguishes sin’s presence from its

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.200
mastery.

5
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.020
Paul tells believers not to let sin

6
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:14.380
reign,

7
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.700
because it still seeks their obedience.

8
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.380
But those united to Christ share

9
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.940
in his death and resurrection.

10
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.840
Their old self was crucified with him.

11
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.880
They belong to a new life.

12
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.380
That is why Paul says to consider

13
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.600
yourselves dead to sin and alive

14
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.180
to God in Christ Jesus.

15
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.560
This means learning to think according

16
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.900
to what God has done.

17
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.140
Temptation does not have the right

18
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:38.980
to command you.

19
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:39.960
When it comes,

20
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.980
remember whose you are.

21
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.420
Offer your words and actions to God

22
00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.480
as someone he has brought from death

23
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.220
to life.
